# source: High-school curriculum inventory, probability direction.
# problem: Find the probability of an even die result and perform a Bayes update.
# proof_idea: Count the uniform event with Chapter 11, then substitute probabilities into Chapter 19.
# litex_code: The two exercises below are the runnable reformulations.
# comments: Original exercise wording; no external textbook prose is copied. Status: checkable by the registered file runner.

# Exercise 1. A fair die lands on an even number with probability one half.
finite_set_size({1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}) = 6
finite_set_size({2, 4, 6}) = 3
{2, 4, 6} $subset {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}
chap11::uniform_probability({1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}, {2, 4, 6}) = 1 / 2

# Exercise 2. Update a prior of 1/3 with likelihood 3/4 and evidence 1/2.
chap19::bayes_posterior(1 / 3, 3 / 4, 1 / 2) = 1 / 2
